 "notes": "The list starts on n42.jpg (p. 27) with 23 rows and continues on n43.jpg (p. 28) with 13 rows, Hanois included: 36 stations in all. n40, n41 and n44 have none of it. The 36 matches the lead-in's \"thirty-six stations\". Six rows are Nil. (Tees Breakwater, Hasbro' L.H., Newarp, Orfordness, Corton, Tongue), which leaves the \"thirty\" stations the text says sent returns.\n\nThe list has two columns only: station, then keepers or Nil. It has no numbers, marks or light characters. The type is printed in small capitals (\"l.h.\", \"l.v.\"); I've written it as \"L.H.\"/\"L.V.\". I left the dotted leaders between the columns out of 'printed'. The stray full stop on some rows (e.g. \"Cockle L.V. .\", \"Corton L.V..\") belongs to those leaders. Each keeper entry ends with a full stop on the page. I kept it in 'printed' and dropped it in 'keepers'. \"Nil.\" is in italics on every row.\n\nKeepers: entries like \"W. Stock and A. Bearling\" name two people with their own initials, so I split them into two entries. Spurn L.V. and East Side L.V. read \"The Principal (no signature).\" That names nobody, so it is in 'other' and 'keepers' is empty. A post was filled there, but we don't know who held it.\n\nCopied as printed, not corrected: \"Llyn Wells\" (usually Lynn Well), \"Hasbro’\" with a curly apostrophe (Happisburgh), \"Languard Point\" (Landguard), \"Orfordness\" as one word, \"Farn, Inner,\" (Inner Farne), and \"Tees, 5 Buoy\" (the 5 is part of the name, not a map number). The surnames \"Bearling\", \"Perfrement\" and \"Westmoreland\" are clear on the scan but should be checked against other years.\n\nHanois L.H., Guernsey is printed at the end of this East Coast list. It is counted among the 36 even though it is in the Channel Islands, so I've given it the East Coast of England heading like the rest.\n\nA separate six-row list follows on n43.jpg under its own lead-in about \"six stations on the South East Coast\". It is not part of this list, so I haven't included it: Dungeness L.H., Royal Sovereign Shoals L.V., Beachy Head L.H., Owers L.V., and St Katherine's L.H., Isle of Wight, all Nil.; Nab L.V., F. Conconi.\n\nThe OCR's garbles (\"Lu.\", \"L.#.\", \"t.v.\", \"L.Vv.\") are all plain L.H./L.V. on the scans. Every word was readable, so no row is marked unsure.",
